格式示例（仅结构，不是来源事实）：evidence:[{"paragraph_id":"p3s1","fact":"该片段支持的中文转述"}]。请从本次真实输入挑选编号。","role":"system"},{"content":"{"metadata":{"description":"DeepSeek Harness 默认 System Prompt 管理插件：在 Web GUI「设置」里浏览、检索并覆盖最终装配进每轮会话的系统提示词","id":"gh:1395875350","install_available":false,"language":"JavaScript","name":"dsh-prompt-setting","slug":"zangxx66/dsh-prompt-setting","topics":["deepseek","deepseek-harness","deepseek-harness-plugin","deepseek-harness-plugins","dsh","dsh-plugin","dsh-plugins"]},"paragraphs":[{"id":"p1s1","text":"DeepSeek Harness 默认 System Prompt 管理插件：在 Web GUI「设置」里浏览、检索并覆盖最终装配进每轮会话的系统提示词"},{"id":"p2s1","text":"# dsh-prompt-setting"},{"id":"p3s1","text":"English | 中文"},{"id":"p4s1","text":"**System Prompt management for DSH (DeepSeek Harness).** It adds a Prompt manager to the Web GUI's\nS"},{"id":"p4s2","text":"ettings: you can **see** the system prompt a session actually assembles on every turn, search it,\nwr"},{"id":"p4s3","text":"ite your own instructions into it, and roll back a bad edit — all **without touching the global DSH\n"},{"id":"p4s4","text":"wn instructions into it, and roll back a bad edit — all **without touching the global DSH\ninstall**."},{"id":"p5s1","text":"- **Zero runtime dependencies, zero build step**: one package of plain JS — nothing to fetch, nothin"},{"id":"p5s2","text":"g to compile.\n- **Upgrade-safe**: configuration is written only to the plugin's own data directory, "},{"id":"p5s3","text":"so upgrading or\nreinstalling DSH neither loses nor overwrites it."},{"id":"p6s1","text":"## 1. What problem this solves"},{"id":"p7s1","text":"Every DSH turn is injected with a base system prompt assembled by `@deepseek-ai/dsh-system-prompt`.\n"},{"id":"p7s2","text":"Until now the only way to adjust it was to **hand-edit files inside the global pnpm `node_modules`**"},{"id":"p7s3","text":"way to adjust it was to **hand-edit files inside the global pnpm `node_modules`**.\nThe cost of that:"},{"id":"p8s1","text":"- the next DSH upgrade overwrites it and your changes are gone;\n- it pollutes a global install, so n"},{"id":"p8s2","text":"obody else — and no other machine — can reproduce it;\n- there is no record of what changed, or of wh"},{"id":"p8s3","text":"at it looked like before;\n- and worst of all, **you cannot see what the finally assembled system pro"},{"id":"p8s4","text":"mpt actually looks like**."},{"id":"p9s1","text":"This plugin moves that into the Settings page: the assembly is laid out section by section, the part"},{"id":"p9s2","text":" you\nwrite is its own section pinned to the end, every other built-in section stays read-only, and c"},{"id":"p9s3","text":"hanges\ncome with history, diffs and exportable backups."},{"id":"p10s1","text":"## 2. What you get after installing"},{"id":"p11s1","text":"Settings gains a **\"Prompt settings\"** pane (`id: prompt-setting`) with six top-level tabs:"},{"id":"p12s1","text":"| Tab | What you can do |"},{"id":"p13s1","text":"| **My Prompt** | The only write surface: write your own system-level instructions (pick a layer → e"},{"id":"p13s2","text":"dit → save), plus a one-click \"Restore default\". This text is **placed after every built-in section*"},{"id":"p13s3","text":"*. The \"View scope\" selector is **inside this panel, under its title** (since g-071): it decides whi"},{"id":"p13s4","text":"ch layer a save lands in, and it is the only place the scope is changed (the panel also repeats the "},{"id":"p13s5","text":"current target as a read-only line). Since g-084 a **read-only two-line status summary** sits under "},{"id":"p13s6","text":"that target line: the latest key node's assembly / delivery verdicts and \"this layer: N override(s) "},{"id":"p13s7","text":"· M not in effect\". It follows \"View scope\" (a global scope says so and borrows no session), \"Detail"},{"id":"p13s8","text":"s\" opens **Advanced** pinned to that session, and it carries **no** switch and no per-entry reason. "},{"id":"p13s9","text":"\"Restore default\" deletes **only this layer's** My Prompt entry and keeps the layer's other override"},{"id":"p13s10","text":"s. |\n| **My presets** | Your catalogue of reusable texts: save a text as a preset (create / edit / d"},{"id":"p13s11","text":"elete), then **apply** it to a workspace (it is written into that workspace layer's reserved section"},{"id":"p13s12","text":") or **cancel** the application, which restores exactly what that workspace held before. Deleting an"},{"id":"p13s13","text":" applied preset **cancels its applications first**: every affected workspace is restored to what it "},{"id":"p13s14","text":"held before, and only then is the preset removed from the library (the confirmation names those work"},{"id":"p13s15","text":"spaces). **Tags** (g-082): the library has its own tag set; a preset may carry 0–N tags and the list"},{"id":"p13s16","text":" filters by one tag at a time. Tags are created, renamed and deleted under \"Manage tags\"; a deletion"},{"id":"p13s17","text":" asks first and states how many presets lose the tag — the presets keep their other tags and only th"},{"id":"p13s18","text":"at tag goes. |\n| **Prompt overview** | Read-only: the assembled section list (status marks / search "},{"id":"p13s19","text":"/ filters / copy), the full text, and a `base ↔ effective` diff — so you can see exactly what your c"},{"id":"p13s20","text":"hange did. |\n[该节后续省略]"},{"id":"p14s1","text":"### Network access: it checks for updates once (and you can turn it off)"},{"id":"p15s1","text":"When the settings page opens, the **host** (Node side) sends one `GET` to\n`https://api.github.com/re"},{"id":"p15s2","text":"pos/zangxx66/dsh-prompt-setting/releases/latest` — a URL derived from this\npackage's `package.json` "},{"id":"p15s3","text":"(`repository.url`), never hardcoded a second time. That is the plugin's\n**only** outbound request, a"},{"id":"p15s4","text":"nd it is switchable:"},{"id":"p16s1","text":"- **one request, nothing else**: no body, no cookies, no local/session/workspace data;\n`User-Agent: "},{"id":"p16s2","text":"dsh-prompt-setting/<version>`; a 5-second timeout; not repeated within six hours in the\nsame process"},{"id":"p16s3","text":";\n- **it speaks up only for a confirmed newer release**: a **dismissible** banner at the top of the "},{"id":"p16s4","text":"page\n(the new version + a link to the release page). No update, no release yet, or a failed request "},{"id":"p16s5","text":"shows\n**nothing at all** at the top of the page — no prompt and no error. \"No release yet / unparsab"},{"id":"p16s6","text":"le tag\" is\na *fact about upstream*, so it gets one neutral line inside the Advanced switch card; a *"},{"id":"p16s7","text":"*failed** check\ndoes not get that line;\n- **turning it off**: Settings → Prompt settings → Advanced "},{"id":"p16s8","text":"→ turn **\"Check for updates\"** off. With it\noff there are **zero requests**, including on page load,"},{"id":"p16s9","text":" and `<DSH_HOME>/prompt-setting/preferences.json`\nrecords `{\"updateCheck\": false}`. Hand-editing tha"},{"id":"p16s10","text":"t file — or deleting it to return to the default\n(on) — works the same way;\n- **what it never does**"},{"id":"p16s11","text":": no automatic download, no automatic install, **no automatic restart**, and no\nDSH platform version"},{"id":"p16s12","text":"tomatic download, no automatic install, **no automatic restart**, and no\nDSH platform version check."},{"id":"p17s1","text":"### Installing the update (\"Update now\")"},{"id":"p18s1","text":"**The version gets installed; the restart is still yours — and the page says how.** The banner's\n**U"},{"id":"p18s2","text":"pdate now** button opens a second confirmation (which says so), and on confirm the **host** installs"},{"id":"p18s3","text":"\nthat release's `.tgz` into the current profile through the official plugin manager. Afterwards the "},{"id":"p18s4","text":"page\nanswers for the **launch shape** it is talking to: a command-line host says \"vX.Y.Z is installe"},{"id":"p18s5","text":"d — restart\n`dsh web` yourself\", the official desktop app says \"quit and reopen DeepSeek Harness\" (a"},{"id":"p18s6","text":" desktop user has\nno terminal, so `dsh web` never appears there), and an undecidable shape falls bac"},{"id":"p18s7","text":"k to copy both readers\ncan follow. **Nothing here restarts anything.**"},{"id":"p19s1","text":"- **what it installs**: the release **asset**\n`https://github.com/zangxx66/dsh-prompt-setting/releas"},{"id":"p19s2","text":"es/download/<tag>/dsh-prompt-setting-<version>.tgz`,\nwith `<tag>`/`<version>` taken from the *same* "},{"id":"p19s3","text":"update check — so the version announced is the version\ninstalled, and a cached check still costs zer"},{"id":"p19s4","text":"o outbound requests. Being an asset, it needs no pnpm\n[该节后续省略]"}],"truncated":true}","role":"user"}],"model":"MiniMax-M3.1-Flash","reasoning_effort":"low","stream":false}
